mantle rm336
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for rm_edric_cindermarsh
title the iron ear
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=smith
traits temper=nervy talk=chatty warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk tests_a_cool_iron_ring_by_humming_its_pitch
likes mutton_stew wrestling fresh_straw frosty_mornings
dislikes stale_bread smoke
fears missing_the_last_clear_note_in_a_ring
hopes to_make_a_hinge_that_opens_in_silence
topics work +0.5 health +0.2 pastimes +0.3 weather +0.2
styles comfort=practical gossip=guarded refuse=soft tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# hums the note of a cooling iron ring and talks over the last faint echo for fear of losing it.

words
oath! = Ring out my iron ear | Quench that echo
saying! = Hear the crack before trusting the ring | The last note belongs to the metal
ring = a cool iron ring | my sample hoop
pin = a bright hinge pin | a little black spindle
note = a short true note | a fading hum
end = the last shiver | the dying vibration
ear = my listening ear | an ear cocked sideways
pot = a heavy stewpot | a cast pot
straw = a twist of new straw | a tuft of dry straw
joint = a smooth wrist hold | a safe elbow grip
rime = a fern of white rime | thin white frost
steam = a thread of steam | a low cloud above the pot
smoke = a smear of black smoke | the bitter reek
crust = a hard bread rind | a leathery crust

any
opinion festivals for 1 : At a festival there's room for a loud wolf and a doubting wolf. Sometimes I can be both in the same coat.
opinion houses against 1 : I'd like a House name to ring as truly under a question as a sound hoop under the lightest tap.
opinion merchants against 1 : A copper here and another there will wear a hole clean through an honest purse.
opinion strangers against 1 : I'd sooner learn what follows a newcomer through the gate before I leave the yard standing wide.
opinion sump against 1 : Down by the Sump too many sounds come back from the wrong direction. My ears get little peace there.

grown
line greet [pair.band=strangers] : You have my good ear. Welcome. | Stand where a word can reach me clean.
line greet [self.working=yes] : I'm listening across my work. | Come within the fall of my voice.
line greet [here.time=dawn] : Morning, before the first clang. | A clear ear at this hour.
line greet [here.time=dusk|night] : Evening. The little sounds begin to carry. | Come in where the day's last note is fading.
line kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : I've known that family sound a long while. | There's kin inside my hearing.
line again.open : An echo back on two feet. | Here's the answering note already.
line greet.return : I hear both consonants. Hello. | You've a good clear carry.
line greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : I'd pick that voice out over a struck hoop. | Stay by the listening shoulder.
line greet.return [self.working=yes] : Let the last note settle first. | I'll put the ring down to hear you.
line greet.return [here.time=dusk|night] : Evening. A voice can carry further now. | The eye's tiring. My ears manage.
line farewell : May your own gate swing sweetly. | Take the quieter turning home.
line farewell.return : I'll hold the echo here. | Good metal beneath your latch.
line farewell.return [here.time=night] : Hear the latch behind you tonight. | Light steps beyond the late fires.
line react.news : What sound did the account make? | Let's hear it from the clear side.
line react.news.new : New pitch to my ear. | That's changed my listening.
line react.news.known : That note's been struck before. | I've heard the full account already.
line react.news.doubt : I'd tap that tale in a different place. | Its ring doesn't quite answer the way I expected.
line react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : There's an ache in hearing that. | Take my quiet corner for a rest.
line react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : A fine note in the day's noise. | That's word worth carrying home warm.
line ask.how : How's the world sounding to you? | Much noise in your head today?
line answer.how : I've an ordinary hum in both ears. | Holding steady, perhaps a shade too loudly.
line decline : I'd rather rest my ears before another task. | I ought to hold my attention for this one.
line accept_decline : Fair note. I accept it. | Then I'll let that sound die.
line thank : You've steadied the ring considerably. | That settles a worry at my end.
line sympathise : I'll stay within a breath of you. | Take the sheltered side of my voice.
line reassure : Some metal rings better after resting. | No call to answer over all the noise.
line preclose : I'll put the sample hoop away. | Time to leave my ears a pause.

scene cold
when topic=work self.job=smith
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : When iron's quite cold I tap #ring# and hum the note.
b : Which sound matters most? | Why hum?
a : A split clips the end short. I want the sound to die naturally. | My own note carries on after the ring stops. I can compare their lengths.

scene hinge
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My wish is for a hinge I never hear working.
b : Wouldn't that deprive you of a note? | For a grand door?
a : The trial ring can sing. A finished hinge has better work to do. | For a bedroom. Sleep is worth the extra work.

scene wrestle
when topic=pastimes self.likes=wrestling
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A wrist hold teaches you a fair bit about metal.
b : They're much alike? | Which part of a hold?
a : Both resent a twist that ignores where the joint actually goes. | The release. An easy opening is the best test of what went in.

scene stew
when topic=food self.likes=mutton_stew
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I listen at the stew before I lift its lid.
b : What do you hear? | Why not look?
a : A big lump of mutton makes the bubbles come up in separate places. | The steam has earned its keep. I leave it inside a while.

scene straw
when topic=home self.likes=fresh_straw
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : New straw under my feet takes the metal note out of a floor.
b : Can you tell through shoes? | Is that restful?
a : More through my ears. A hollow board loses its click. | After a working day I'd sooner hear straw bending than iron singing.

scene frost
when topic=weather self.likes=frosty_mornings
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Frost finds every scratch in a gate.
b : Does it get in the hinge? | How can you tell?
a : Along the edges if they're rough. I keep the moving face clean. | Two white lines where yesterday the eye saw solid black.

scene smoke
when topic=health self.dislikes=smoke
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Smoke takes my voice before it takes my working hands.
b : Can't you still hum? | What do you do?
a : I can, but it comes back rough and tells me nothing about the metal. | Get to clear air before trying to prove anything.

scene stale
when topic=food self.dislikes=stale_bread
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : If I knock a bread heel and hear it ring I've bought too late.
b : Would you take it back? | What if it's just the crust?
a : I'd soak it and remember the shelf next time. | Then the middle will forgive a dip in mutton broth.

scene friend
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd ask #self.friend# to stand a few steps away when I sound a ring.
b : For safety? | What would that tell you?
a : For an ear that isn't already buzzing from my own voice. | How much reaches the other side of a room.

scene secret
when topic=gossip
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I don't care to name a wolf because an ugly rumour resounds.
b : Too doubtful? | Would you even listen?
a : Especially when the telling gets louder each time. Noise can lend a weak thing weight. | For what was actually seen, yes. The rest stays out of my account.

scene works
when topic=home self.quarter=works
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : In the Works I can tell which way I'm facing without opening my eyes fully.
b : From the sound? | Even on a quiet day?
a : Listen for where the wall gives a hammer stroke back to its owner. | I need one sound to get me started. My own heel will do.

scene edge
when topic=work self.job=smith self.workplace
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : At #self.workplace# I keep one finished ring aside for comparison.
b : Not to sell? | How long for?
a : It's mine to question when my ears aren't certain what they've heard. | Until I begin doubting the sample as well. Then I get an independent ear.

scene temper
when topic=day
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Sometimes I talk right over the quiet thing I'm trying to hear.
b : How can you tell? | Does anybody mind?
a : I stop and there's a note underneath, still going quite patiently. | I rather expect so. I try to catch myself before the best part goes.

scene newcomer
when topic=newcomer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I give a strange voice some time before I trust the weight behind it.
b : How much time? | Doesn't that sound hard?
a : I listen until there's no reason to impress anybody. | Perhaps it is. I can still be courteous while my ears decide.

scene rain
when topic=weather
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A little fine rain makes iron go dark unevenly.
b : Where first? | Is dark iron spoiled?
a : In the scratches. A smooth rim keeps reflecting the sky awhile. | No. I dry it properly when I'm through looking, that's all.

scene market
when topic=prices
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I weigh an iron ring without making a customer admire the sound first.
b : To be fair? | Is it a bad sound?
a : A pleasing sound is liable to make a modest piece of work seem dearer. | Sometimes excellent. Let the metal earn praise after the price is plain.

scene dreamnote
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I dreamed a hinge was singing louder with every opening.
b : Did you oil it? | Where was the door?
a : I tried. It swallowed the oil like a singer drinking tea and carried on. | Right between two furrows. Even asleep I thought that rather excessive.

scene old
when topic=memories
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I remember hearing a sound linger in a hoop I had put down.
b : Did it roll? | Could you see it move?
a : No, it leaned on one edge against a board and sang through the grain. | Barely. That made the note more striking than any great show of movement.

story potlid [topic=food]
  : I once mended a pot lid that had a very piercing whistle. I flattened the bent rim with confident taps and put it back over the stew.
  : It whistled a lower note. In trying to remove a whistle I'd tuned it instead. I had to sit through supper considering the difference.
  b : What did you change afterwards?
  : A single high spot in a series of very small shifts. The stew only murmurs now.

story strawbed [topic=memories]
  : I took my sample ring home and laid it on the newly strewn floor. I meant to hear whether a quiet room would give it a longer voice.
  : The straw swallowed the first tap. There was scarcely enough sound to tell it was metal. I lifted it onto my thumb and it rang beautifully.
  b : Was anything wrong with the ring?
  : Only the listener's arrangement. I've tried to remember that before blaming a poor note on anybody else.

story hold [topic=pastimes self.likes=wrestling]
  : I once set out to practise a wrestler's footwork wearing my ordinary heavy shoes. The first heel came down exactly on the corner of a spare board.
  : The board bounced. I heard a most interesting vibration and quite forgot to finish my impressive little sequence.
  b : Did you fall?
  : I ended up sitting. Good position for examining a board, if less admired in wrestling.

rule @aside1
when concept=bark self.job=smith self.working=yes
does aside
cooldown 6h
say Hush now. Catch the last shiver. | Cool ring first, sample hoop second.

rule @aside2
when concept=bark self.likes=wrestling
does aside
cooldown 7h
say Keep the elbow where it bends kindly. | Footwork first. Show later.

rule @aside3
when concept=bark self.likes=fresh_straw
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Fresh straw takes the click out beautifully. | A quiet floor for a tired ear.

rule @aside4
when concept=bark here.time=dusk
does aside
cooldown 9h
say There goes the little evening hum. | Put the hoop where it can't roll.

dlg resident.hub : Stand off my shoulder a little. My voice carries quite well, particularly when I intend a particularly quiet point.
dlg resident.job [self.job=smith self.workplace] : At #self.workplace# I work iron and listen to what the iron says afterwards.
dlg resident.news [world.news] : The part that rang clear came to me like this. #world.news#
dlg resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, your voice has a familiar ring to it.
dlg resident.bye : May the latch welcome you without waking the house.

graft resident.hub
choice Why hum back to a ring of iron? -> iron_answer
node iron_answer
say I can just hear the ring at the start, well enough to take up the note. When I stop humming I can tell whether the iron's still carrying on by itself.
free
choice And if the sound drops away? -> iron_stop
choice I'll listen beyond the first tap. -> hub
node iron_stop
say First I find the metal's resting place. A perfectly sound ring pressed against a sleeve will answer as poorly as a cracked one.
choice I'll give the iron room. -> hub
choice I leave you the quieter ear. -> bye
